step Fray Island
  zone The Barrens
  tip Fly to Ratchet and go south along the Merchant Coast. Fray Island lies offshore to the south-east: wade across on the shallow sand bar; off it the water is deep and fatigue sets in. Klannoc Macleod stands by the arena.
  turnin 1718                                 -- Klannoc Macleod
  accept 1719

step The Affray
  tip You have 10 minutes. Eat and drink to full, then step onto the grate in the middle of the crowd: Twiggy Flathead announces the challengers (level 26-27), who come one at a time, 15-20 seconds apart, and only while you stand near the grate. After each kill, step off the grate to eat or bandage; step back on when ready for the next. Six of them, then Big Will (level 33, not elite) walks out; he stays neutral until you attack him, so bandage or eat first. Do not use Demoralizing Shout: it sends the challengers running and more of them pile in at once. If nothing starts, step off and on the grate again, or abandon the quest and take it again.
  kill 6238 quest 1719.1 @68.6,48.7           -- Big Will
  turnin 1719                                 -- Klannoc Macleod: Berserker Stance
  accept 1791

step Bath'rah the Windwatcher
  zone Alterac Mountains
  tip Bath'rah the Windwatcher camps by ruins on the east bank of the river that runs past Tarren Mill, a short walk north-east of the town, just over the border in Alterac Mountains; his cauldron stands beside him. Horde: fly to Tarren Mill. Alliance: fly to Southshore and go north along the river; Tarren Mill's guards are level 42 elites, so keep away from the town. Accepting Cyclonian gives you Bath'rah's Parchment, the list of what he needs: 8 Liferoot, 30 Bloodscalp Tusks and the Essence of the Exile from his cauldron. Click the cauldron for that quest.
  turnin 1791                                 -- Bath'rah the Windwatcher
  accept 1712
  accept 1714 object 89931                    -- Bath'rah's Cauldron

step The exiles of Arathi
  zone Arathi Highlands
  tip The cauldron wants 8 of each charm, 24 in all, and each exile drops its charm about one kill in three, so plan on some 70 kills. All are level 38-39, not elite, and hit hard at 30-33: bring a friend or come at 35 or more. Burning Exiles (fire) by the Circle of West Binding in the north-west, north-west of Refuge Pointe; Thundering Exiles (air) by the Circle of Outer Binding south-east of Refuge Pointe, casting Lightning Bolt from 40 yards; Cresting Exiles (water) by the Circle of East Binding, north-west of Hammerfall, with Frost Nova. About a dozen of each, back in under 7 minutes. The charms trade and sell on the auction house; using one banishes another kind of exile for a while (Burning on Thundering, Thundering on Cresting, Cresting on Burning).
  collect 4479 x8 quest 1714.2                -- Burning Charm, from Burning Exiles
  collect 4480 x8 quest 1714.1                -- Thundering Charm, from Thundering Exiles
  collect 4481 x8 quest 1714.3                -- Cresting Charm, from Cresting Exiles

step Essence of the Exile
  zone Alterac Mountains
  tip Put the 24 charms into Bath'rah's Cauldron: it hands you the Essence of the Exile.
  turnin 1714 object 89931                    -- Bath'rah's Cauldron: Essence of the Exile
  collect 6851 quest 1712.3 @80.5,66.9        -- Essence of the Exile, from the cauldron by Bath'rah

step Liferoot
  tip You need 8 Liferoot. Herbalists pick it by rivers and lakes in the Wetlands, Arathi Highlands and Stranglethorn Vale; otherwise the auction house. Herb vendors keep only one at a time and restock every two hours: Bernard Gump and Maria Lumere in Stormwind, Antonio Perelli on the road in eastern Elwynn, Jeeda at Sun Rock Retreat in Stonetalon, Montarr in Thousand Needles. Kurzen Medicine Men in northern Stranglethorn drop one about one kill in twelve.
  collect 3357 x8 quest 1712.1                -- Liferoot

step Bloodscalp Tusks
  zone Stranglethorn Vale
  tip You need 30 tusks. Every Bloodscalp troll (level 33-37) of north-west Stranglethorn drops one about one kill in three, so plan on some 80 kills: the camps and ruins north and north-west of Grom'gol Base Camp and around the Bal'lal Ruins on the coast. They enrage below 30% health and the Warriors disarm; back in 5 minutes.
  collect 3901 x30 quest 1712.2               -- Bloodscalp Tusk

step The Summoning
  zone Alterac Mountains
  tip Back to Bath'rah. Accepting The Summoning starts his ritual, and Cyclonian appears just north of his camp. Cyclonian is elite (level 40): grouping up is encouraged; it needs a group of two or three around level 40. It deals nature damage (a Nature Protection Potion soaks it), whirls, and Knock Away throws you far while it heals itself as you run back: fight with your back to a slope or rock. The Whirlwind Heart always drops. If the fight fails Bath'rah stops answering: abandon The Summoning and take it again for a new summon; the earlier items are not needed again.
  turnin 1712                                 -- Bath'rah the Windwatcher
  accept 1713
  kill 6239 group 3                           -- Cyclonian
  collect 6894 quest 1713.1                   -- Whirlwind Heart, from Cyclonian
  turnin 1713
  accept 1792
  turnin 1792 choose 6975 6977 6976           -- Bath'rah the Windwatcher: Whirlwind Axe, Sword or Warhammer
